{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/weight-loss/rucking-results-what-to-expect", "version_id": "0ae0d0a592ed77ea68c9223b5a62c8f9ab03f2ad94f7c9a850674658577efb93", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is a weight-loss timeline and calorie-arithmetic article rather than a gear item, and its only gear content is a passing recommendation of socks, anti-chafe, and a watch. Under Credibility and Commercial incentives, it is a publisher with affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and the body's own corrections admit prior unsupported monthly forecasts, so it does not meet the Unsupported claims or Making the decision standards for an accepted gear item.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/goruck-mackall-45-first-look", "version_id": "1b660b68127b0a769054c99615a30cf590fc83693faafcf0080a51f151655cd6", "decision": "defer", "reason": "Under Relevance this is a footwear review for rucking, which is in scope, but under Credibility and Commercial incentives it is a single-reviewer review of a GORUCK-supplied pair with affiliate commissions, and its evidence rests on one tester's first outing and a later walk with a loaded GR1 and 20 lb plate. The Mackall 45 is not supported by three independent publishers, and the article itself cites other reviewers only as accounts of different colorways, so the central durability and performance claims are too thin to rely on yet under the Uncertainty rule.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/goruck-tough-packing-list", "version_id": "195e0f4d26f7b3bee7622b1fda745e363711bd456feb57f99cc78333e3681e5a", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Making the decision, this is a promotional packing-list and product-recommendation post that is heavily tied to GORUCK, with GORUCK-supplied units, affiliate commissions, and a shop-linked event kit, so it offers no substantive independent testing evidence. Its official-requirement content (the GORUCK registration page checked August 31, 2026) is a directly cited event requirement, but the article is largely an unsourced editorial product selection that the Commercial incentives and Unsupported claims rules do not let us accept as a gear review.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/rucking-for-weight-loss-gear-guide", "version_id": "075cca7b7d290eef48c929410460f6daa548faa2009d56719ebfb401adddb3bd", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Making the decision and Commercial incentives, this is a shopping guide built around product cards and a starter kit with affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and its weight-loss calorie claims rely on a model it admits under-predicts energy use, so it is promotional rather than substantive evidence. It contains no independent field testing that would support the Credibility and Unsupported claims rules, and its gear picks are editorial selections rather than tested findings.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/goruck-labor-day-sale-2026", "version_id": "7b116c31175b02094b025a82f3cf6d2b300c9a903c7e2d55437dabe10d57856f", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance and Exclusions, this is a sales and deals post about GORUCK markdowns and a holiday promotion, which the policy expressly rejects. It is also stale relative to the 2026-10-15 date, since the Labor Day window ended September 7 and the article itself says its offers may no longer be available.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/rucking-fitness-trend-2026", "version_id": "06a1df5ae4472364410f48fdc0260569502ca36887afc51f46a95c67c1368d18", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is trend commentary and a how-to-start guide rather than a review of gear in scope, and under Credibility and Commercial incentives its trend claims rest on a fitness-trend roundup, a company's own sales figure, and an unnamed high-profile endorsement rather than independent testing. Under Unsupported claims the article's growth and longevity assertions lack the evidence the policy requires, and its gear mentions are incidental and affiliate-linked, so it does not meet the bar for an accepted item.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/rucking-for-bone-density", "version_id": "586dc303595281ba26e8e1470d2bbd63cbc7482e7806b2810b7d177cbfcdd5ce", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is a bone-health and training-guidance article whose gear content is limited to a CAP vest and plate mentions, and it is not a gear evaluation of the kind the policy accepts. Under Unsupported claims and Credibility, its research summaries are generally careful, but the article is not a test of gear and offers no independent field evidence about any product's suitability or effectiveness at Mammoth, so it falls outside the accept standard.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/rucking-for-mental-health", "version_id": "1ac6d2379c4d9d6a74417c5ccbc9f4c88cfee9a8f007563c5b932e571a619ee5", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is a mental-health article about walking and rucking rather than a gear item, and it contains no product testing in scope for the three pieces. Under Making the decision, its only gear content is a generic starter list and affiliate-linked guide references, so it is unconnected to the gear evaluation the publication exists to serve.", "piece_ids": []}
